00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.789 align:start position:0%
this is the coastal town of mangla near  the bay of bengal it's part of an  ambitious plan by the bangladeshi  government to transform this area into a  refuge for those displaced by climate  change there are several other similar  towns around the country  sonya begum and her family are among the  many here who were forced to move here  to find jobs and a safer place to live  our village home was destroyed by a  storm so we moved here  even before there were too many  weather-related problems and it wasn't a  good place to live anymore we do face  some problems with commuting and getting  enough fresh water but it's much better  here  bangladesh already invests about three  billion dollar a year to address the  effect of climate change  in recent years bangladesh government  have spent considerable amount of  resources in developing mangala as a  climate model town it has invested in  businesses industries power plants and  other facilities as well as attract  foreign investment  the town's mayor sheikh abdulrahman says  there are other projects underway to  make life easier for people here that  includes an airport and the construction  of a rail line to connect the town to an  economic hub across the border in india  ships are coming trade is going on goods  are being produced and new jobs are  being created mongolia's port is active  which is why people are better off here  but rahman says much more still needs to  be done to help people who have been  displaced by climate change  the nearby rural areas suffered heavily  due to climate change river erosion and  high salinity have affected the farming  and shrimp cultivation which is why many  rural migrants are now settling in  mongol town  many women are able to find jobs here  and support their family  since the export processing zone and  other industries opened here it's become  easier to find jobs there weren't many  job opportunities before we've been  living here ever since we lost our home  in a storm  bangladesh has one of the fastest  growing economies in asia but the  climate-induced internal displacement  has become one of its biggest challenges  a model town like mangla offers some  hope and shows how those who have been  displaced by climate change can  transform their lives through new  initiatives and opportunities tanvi  choudhary al-jazeera bangla bangladesh
 

